						key="staticText-2"/>
					<box></box>
					<textElement markup="html" lineSpacing="Single">
						<font size="10"/>
					</textElement>
				<text><![CDATA[<b>Loans of Herbarium Specimens</b>
<br/>
Terms and Conditions
<ul>
<li>In order to ensure the preservation of our specimen collections certain restrictions apply to all loan requests.</li>
<br/>
<li>It is the responsibility of the user to comply with Access and Benefits Sharing requirements from the country of origin and if the sample was collected after the 12th of October 2014 from a country that has ratified the Nagoya Protocol.  Refer to the Access and Benefit -Sharing Clearing-House absch.cbd.int for more information.</li>
<br/>
<li>The Herbarium at RBGE will only consider loans from recognised institutes and not from individuals.  All loan requests should come from the Curator or Director of the researcher’s institute.</li>
<br/>
<li>Loans are normally issued for a period of 12 months only. Type specimens are issued for a period of 6 months only.  An extension to this period may be granted following a written request.</li>
<br/>
<li>Loans should be returned securely packed to ensure safe transit.  A shipping notice should be included with each returned loan.</li>
<br/>
<li>The permanent removal of any part of the specimen on loan for palynological, anatomical, phytochemical or molecular work is not permitted without obtaining prior permission.  If the study requires destructive sampling a special request may be submitted.  Please see our Destructive Sampling policy for more information; it is found on our website.   www.rbge.org.uk/science/herbarium</li>
<br/>
<li>Specimens on loan should be stored in suitable conditions to ensure that no specimen is damaged whilst in the researcher’s institute.  Specimens should not be removed from the researcher’s institute whilst on loan.</li>
<br/>
<li>Please annotate specimens with appropriate slips before returning the loan (e.g. Determinavit, Confirmavit, Fide….).  These should be attached with archival quality adhesives or with a paper clip.</li>
<br/>
<li>Publications which include specimens loaned from RBGE should include an acknowledgement and, where possible, a copy should be sent to the Herbarium Office at RBGE.  herbarium@rbge.org.uk</li>
</ul>
<br/>
<br/>
For Data Protection guidance please see website http://rbge.org.uk/privacy]]></text>
				</staticText>
